6. Entity and Enums

CustomerKyc.java represents the CUSTOMER_KYC Oracle table. The Java fields map to database columns using JPA annotations.

@Entity
@Table(name = "CUSTOMER_KYC")
public class CustomerKyc {
    private Long kycId;
    private Long customerId;
    private KycStatus kycStatus;
    private DocumentType documentType;
    private String documentNumber;
    private LocalDateTime verifiedAt;
    private LocalDateTime lastReviewedAt;
    private LocalDateTime createdAt;
    private LocalDateTime updatedAt;
}

Enums make KYC values type-safe:

KycStatus:
PENDING
VERIFIED
REJECTED
REVIEW_REQUIRED

DocumentType:
PASSPORT
DRIVER_LICENSE
STATE_ID
SSN

7. DTOs

CustomerKycRequest is used when creating KYC:

{
  "documentType": "DRIVER_LICENSE",
  "documentNumber": "TX12345678"
}

The client does not send kycId, status, timestamps, or customer lifecycle fields. Those are controlled by the backend.

CustomerKycStatusRequest is used only for status changes:

{
  "kycStatus": "VERIFIED"
}

CustomerKycResponse controls the data returned to the API client.

8. Repository

Optional<CustomerKyc> findByCustomerId(Long customerId);

boolean existsByCustomerId(Long customerId);

Spring Data JPA derives queries from these method names. findByCustomerId retrieves a customer's KYC record, while existsByCustomerId supports duplicate prevention.

9. Service Business Logic

Create KYC flow:

Customer ID
   ↓
Find customer
   ↓
Customer exists?
   ↓
Customer is ACTIVE?
   ↓
KYC already exists?
   ↓
Create KYC with PENDING status
   ↓
Save through repository
   ↓
Return response DTO

CustomerNotFoundException is thrown if the customer does not exist.

KycCustomerInactiveException is thrown if the customer is INACTIVE.

DuplicateCustomerKycException is thrown if a KYC row already exists.

KYC starts as PENDING.

Status update sets lastReviewedAt and updatedAt.

VERIFIED also sets verifiedAt.

Other statuses clear verifiedAt in the current implementation.

The active-customer check uses the enum directly:

if (customer.getCustomerStatus() != CustomerStatus.ACTIVE) {
    throw new KycCustomerInactiveException(
        "KYC can be created only for active customers"
    );
}

