17. Interview Explanation

On Day 11, I extended Customer Service with a KYC module. I created a Flyway-managed CUSTOMER_KYC table in Oracle, mapped it with a JPA entity, and used separate DTOs for creation, status updates, and API responses. The service layer enforces business rules such as active-customer validation, one KYC record per customer, initial PENDING status, and verification timestamps. Spring Data JPA handles persistence, custom exceptions integrate with our standardized error contract, and Swagger exposes the KYC APIs for interactive testing. I also added Mockito unit tests and verified the main positive and negative flows in Postman.

18. Day 11 Result

Customer Service now supports a structured KYC lifecycle in addition to customer profile and address history. This prepares the platform for future account-opening rules, compliance workflows, S3 document storage, security/RBAC, notifications, and reporting.